# Authentication Test Cases and Results

## Scope and environment
- Branch: `feature/issue-7-auth-tests`
- App: Hope, Inc. info management app
- Stack: Next.js + Supabase Auth
- Local environment: `.env.local` is configured for the development Supabase project
- DB migration: confirmed by the DB Admin as applied
- No test accounts were created during these checks
- Product decision: passwords do not expire; old passwords should remain usable unless a separate expiry policy is introduced

## Executed checks

| ID | Check | Expected result | Actual result | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| BUILD-01 | Run `npm run build` | Production build completes successfully | Build succeeded | PASS |
| TYPE-01 | Run `npm run typecheck` | No TypeScript errors | Type check passed | PASS |
| ROUTE-01 | Open `/`, `/sign-in`, `/register`, `/reset-password`, `/set-password` | Pages load correctly | All returned HTTP 200 | PASS |
| ROUTE-02 | Open `/account` and `/admin/approvals` without a signed-in session | Redirect to sign-in | Both returned HTTP 307 | PASS |
| ROUTE-03 | Open `/auth/callback` and `/auth/confirm` without a token/code | Invalid auth callback is rejected | Both returned HTTP 307 | PASS |
| DB-01 | Call `/api/health` | Database is connected | HTTP 200 with database status `"connected"` | PASS |

